  "description": "EVO Word to PDF Library for .NET (Classic) can be used in .NET Framework, .NET Core and .NET Standard applications on Windows to convert Word (.doc, .docx) and RTF documents to PDF.\n\nFor Windows, Linux and macOS, on x64 and ARM64, EvoPdf Next converts Word DOCX documents to PDF with the multi-platform package EvoPdf.Next.WordToPdf and the platform packages EvoPdf.Next.WordToPdf.Windows, EvoPdf.Next.WordToPdf.Windows.Arm64, EvoPdf.Next.WordToPdf.Linux, EvoPdf.Next.WordToPdf.Linux.Arm64 and EvoPdf.Next.WordToPdf.MacOS.\n\nRTF documents are converted with EvoPdf.Next.RtfToPdf and the platform packages EvoPdf.Next.RtfToPdf.Windows, EvoPdf.Next.RtfToPdf.Windows.Arm64, EvoPdf.Next.RtfToPdf.Linux, EvoPdf.Next.RtfToPdf.Linux.Arm64 and EvoPdf.Next.RtfToPdf.MacOS.\n\nThe full EvoPdf Next library, which also converts HTML, Excel and Markdown to PDF, comes in the EvoPdf.Next, EvoPdf.Next.Windows, EvoPdf.Next.Windows.Arm64, EvoPdf.Next.Linux, EvoPdf.Next.Linux.Arm64 and EvoPdf.Next.MacOS packages.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* .NET Framework 4.0 and above\n* .NET 10, 9, 8, 7, 6 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* Windows platforms\n* Azure Cloud Services and Azure Virtual Machines\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert Word DOC, DOCX and RTF documents to PDF\n* Does not require Microsoft Word or other third-party tools\n* Convert to a memory buffer, file, stream or PDF object\n* Convert all pages or only selected pages\n* Add headers and footers with page numbering to PDF pages\n* Append or prepend external PDF files to the result\n* Password-protect and digitally sign PDF documents\n* Add graphic elements to the PDF pages\n* Generate PDF/A and PDF/X compliant documents\n* Generate CMYK and grayscale PDF documents\n* Edit, merge and split PDF documents",
  "iconFile": "images\\icon.png",
